It works! Thank you =)
As an additional note: as
almost
always, this is not compatible with Visustella_core, since the latter modifies the "screen shake" function, leaving it as "random" by default. However, in the same plugin, you can select "original" (the one from RPG Maker MZ) for the default screen shake, which will allow the plugin's "no screen shake" effect to work.
Now, just out of curiosity, do you think there’s a “simple” way to make it compatible with Visustella_core’s screen shake? I like that it’s random rather than just moving from left to right.
If not, I’ll have to decide whether to give up on Visustella's shake effect to get the effect I want, or leave out the plugin you made. Either way, you’ve helped me with what I was looking for, since now I have an option! Thanks a million! =)

